{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\nuse std::path::PathBuf;\nuse serde::{Serialize, de::DeserializeOwned};\nuse habeas_sdk::graph::{CriterionPath, NodePath, Record};\n\n/// A directory of JSON records. Send + Sync; load/store futures are Send.\n/// Defined in habeas_sdk::storage.\npub struct FileEvidenceStorage { /* private fields */ }\n\npub enum FileStorageError {\n    Io(std::io::Error),\n    Json(serde_json::Error),\n}\n\nimpl FileEvidenceStorage {\n    /// Retain the root directory without performing filesystem I/O.\n    pub fn new(root: impl Into<PathBuf>) -> Self;\n\n    /// Deserialize a record, or return None if its file is missing.\n    pub async fn load<N, L>(\n        &self,\n        path: &NodePath,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n    ) -> Result<Option<Record<N, L>>, FileStorageError>\n    where\n        N: DeserializeOwned + Send,\n        L: DeserializeOwned + Send;\n\n    /// Atomically replace this source/criterion pair's record.\n    pub async fn store<N, L>(\n        &self,\n        path: &NodePath,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n        record: &Record<N, L>,\n    ) -> Result<(), FileStorageError>\n    where\n        N: Serialize + Sync,\n        L: Serialize + Sync;\n}\n```\n\n`Record`, `Dependency`, and `Fingerprint` support Serde when their type\nparameters do. `Validation::Ok` is always serializable; its JSON value is\nalready in the record. Serialization bounds on node identities and edge labels\nbelong to this helper's use, rather than `Graph` itself.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs` cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.filesystem-storage.interface`. I did not read the implementation. I read the test helpers `record` and `criterion` and the `StoredGraph` fixture. I also read the `Record`, `Dependency` and `Fingerprint` definitions in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs`.\n\n- **`new` retains the root without I/O.** `paths_are_injective_and_loading_missing_records_has_no_side_effects` builds the store on a root that does not exist. It loads seven different node paths and then asserts `!root.exists()`, so a `new` or `load` that touched the filesystem would fail. `send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys` asserts `!root.exists()` right after `new`.\n- **`load` returns `None` for a missing file.** The same test asserts `is_none()` for every path case. `consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path` asserts it for a fresh node and for a different, unstored node.\n- **`load` deserializes a record.**\n  - `records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error` round-trips a `Record<String, ()>` and checks `revision`, `dependencies` and `output`.\n  - The same test round-trips a `Record<String, String>` that uses `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` with a non-unit label.\n  - This covers both `Dependency` variants and `Fingerprint`, through the `record` helper and the labeled record.\n  - It shows that `Record`, `Dependency` and `Fingerprint` support Serde when their type parameters do, including a non-trivial `L`.\n  - `Validation::Ok` and its JSON value are covered because `Record.output` is a `serde_json::Value`. The tests store and load a `Value` with nested metadata.\n- **`FileStorageError::Json` and `FileStorageError::Io`.**\n  - A node-type mismatch (`u8`) and a label-type mismatch (`u8`) both yield `Json`.\n  - Malformed bytes yield `Json`, and the test checks that the error's string equals the cause's string.\n  - A directory at the record path yields `Io`, checked the same way.\n  - An over-long path component yields `Io` from both `load` and `store`.\n  - The delegation test also checks `Json` for corrupt data.\n- **`store` atomically replaces the record.** `concurrent_readers_only_observe_complete_records_from_competing_writes` runs two writers that each store 30 times, alongside a reader.\n  - Each read must be a complete record: either the initial one, or a record whose revision, dependencies and 8192-character padding all match one writer's id.\n  - The test asserts that exactly one directory entry remains, so no temporary files are left behind.\n  - A truncate-then-write implementation would be likely to fail the reader's assertions.\n- **`store` creates a missing root and nested directories.** This is checked in the send-futures test, which stores under a root that does not exist yet and asserts the record file exists.\n- **`Send + Sync` and `Send` futures.**\n  - The send-futures test passes the `store` and `load` futures through `send<T: Send>`, which checks at compile time that they are `Send`.\n  - The concurrent test shares an `Arc<FileEvidenceStorage>` across scoped threads, which requires the type to be `Send + Sync`.\n- **Serialization bounds belong to the helper.** `StoredGraph` is a `Graph` with `String` ids and `()` labels, and it delegates to the store. This shows the bounds are met by the helper's use.\n\nI found no obligation of this requirement without a test, and no assertion that contradicts it. I found no `{fixme}` acknowledgments, and none are needed.",
